  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Lion's Teeth** (1 review): Jeff McLeod's drumming adds a more visceral feel and heightens the emotional energy of this song [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Alpha Double Negative: Going to Catalina**: rare: 12 archived performances [5]\n- **Black Molly**: back after 23 archived shows (496 days) [5]\n- **New Star Song**: back after 52 archived shows (2626 days) [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2005-06-20** (recommended): source not stated; 17 songs; 69 min; rated 4.67/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the recording's sound quality superb; Sound is mediocre: noticeable audience noise, indistinct guitar, and a muffled vocal [2][4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Features entertaining stage commentary from the band and some amusing remarks from the audience [2]\n- Reviewer asks whether the taper also recorded the Doug Fir Lounge shows on 6/10/06, 3/3/07 and 3/8/07 [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2005-06-20**: taped by Peter Sohriakoff; source: Core Sound Binaurial Microphones (CSB's) > Sony Hi-MD MZ-RH10 (1.4mbps PCM ) [1]",
